    "bubble": {
      "word": "BUBBLE",
      "definitions": [
        {
          "text": "A thin film of liquid inflated with air or gas; as, a soap bubble; bubbles on the surface of a river. Beads of sweat have stood upon thy brow, Like bubbles in a late disturbed stream. Shak.",
          "partOfSpeech": "noun"
        },
        {
          "text": "A small quantity of air or gas within a liquid body; as, bubbles rising in champagne or aërated waters.",
          "partOfSpeech": "noun"
        },
        {
          "text": "A globule of air, or globular vacuum, in a transparent solid; as, bubbles in window glass, or in a lens.",
          "partOfSpeech": "noun"
        },
        {
          "text": "A small, hollow, floating bead or globe, formerly used for testing the strength of spirits.",
          "partOfSpeech": "noun"
        },
        {
          "text": "The globule of air in the spirit tube of a level.",
          "partOfSpeech": "noun"
        },
        {
          "text": "Anything that wants firmness or solidity; that which is more specious than real; a false show; a cheat or fraud; a delusive scheme; an empty project; a dishonest speculation; as, the South Sea bubble. Then a soldier . . . Seeking the bubble reputation Even in the cannon's mouth. Shak.",
          "partOfSpeech": "noun"
        },
        {
          "text": "A person deceived by an empty project; a gull. [Obs.] \"Ganny's a cheat, and I'm a bubble.\" Prior.",
          "partOfSpeech": "noun"
        },
        {
          "text": "To rise in bubbles, as liquids when boiling or agitated; to contain bubbles. The milk that bubbled in the pail. Tennyson.",
          "partOfSpeech": "verb"
        },
        {
          "text": "To run with a gurdling noise, as if forming bubbles; as, a bubbling stream. Pope.",
          "partOfSpeech": "verb"
        },
        {
          "text": "To sing with a gurgling or warbling sound. At mine ear Bubbled the nightingale and heeded not. Tennyson.",
          "partOfSpeech": "verb"
        }
      ],
